Package: bmeas
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Hierarchical Measurement Modeling
Version: 0.0.47.9000
Authors@R: person("Prototype", "Contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "prototype@example.invalid")
Description: Bayesian hierarchical measurement modeling combining flexible
    response models, including standard statistical distributions and
    cognitive-model likelihoods, with user-specified latent measurement
    structures. Individual-level model parameters, factor loadings, latent
    traits, and their correlations are estimated jointly from the observed
    data, allowing parameter-estimation uncertainty to be carried through the
    measurement model. The framework accommodates structures ranging from
    simple factor models to decompositions of individual differences into
    general and domain-specific components. Current computation and validation
    cover explicitly documented subsets.
